# EventAI's action_type -> the MAI verb it means, and where each of its three
# columns goes.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. Lowering a `dbscripts_on_*` row is forty generic
# lines: actions.manifest was extracted from `ScriptInfo`'s union, so a row's
# datalongs ARE the verb's parameters, in order, and a loop copies them. An
# EventAI action is a DIFFERENT union describing the same verbs, and the two
# disagree constantly:
#
#     cast          is (spell, TARGET, flags) here and (spell, flags) there
#     remove_aura   is (TARGET, spell) here and (spell) there -- reversed
#     morph         takes an entry AND a model id here, one field plus a flag
#                   there
#
# A positional loop gets all three wrong, and wrong SILENTLY: every column is a
# uint32, every value loads, and the only symptom is a creature casting with the
# wrong flags in a dungeon nobody has run this month. It is not a hypothetical.
# The first conversion of this table was positional, and on a live world's own
# data it put a target selector into the cast flags of 6,556 rows, dropped the
# real cast flags of 3,873, gave 793 summons a despawn delay of 1 millisecond,
# and turned all 71 `remove_aura` rows into "remove aura 0".
#
# WHY IT IS A MANIFEST AND NOT A TABLE IN THE CODE. Two things need this
# mapping and they are written in different languages: the SQL conversion
# (tools/convert_eventai.py), which writes `mai_rule` once, and the C++
# lowering (MaiRuleLowering.cpp), which converts at load while the old tables
# are still what gets read. Two copies of a fifty-row table WILL drift, and the
# drift is invisible for the same reason the original bug was. So it is
# declared once, here; the generator emits the C++ half; and the ctest that
# checks the other manifests checks this one.
#
# THE SELECTOR IS NOT A PARAMETER. It is the same concept in a different column
# per verb, which is why it comes out of the operands entirely and onto the
# Step, next to the buddy. See MaiScript.h.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SYNTAX
#
#     action <type> <verb>  <p1> <p2> <p3>  [extra...]
#
# where each of p1..p3 is one of:
#
#     <name>      a parameter of that verb, BY NAME. Checked against
#                 actions.manifest, so renaming or reordering a parameter there
#                 fails the build instead of silently transposing two columns.
#     select      this column is the target selector
#     -           EventAI does not use this column
#
# and each extra is one of:
#
#     buddy_as_target   the creature acts ON the selected unit (`cast`), rather
#                       than the selected unit BEING the actor (`set_unit_field`)
#     <name>=<value>    pin a parameter the row does not carry
#     form=<name>       a shape no column mapping can express; see below
#
#     form=entry_or_model   two columns, one slot: an entry in the first or a
#                           model id in the second, and the DB-script verb says
#                           which it holds with a flag
#     form=summon_spawn     the third column is a spawn id naming a row in
#                           `creature_ai_summons`, which holds the position and
#                           the despawn time
#
#     refuse <type> <reason>
#
# A refused type is one no MAI verb can express faithfully. Every one below is
# a question for actions.manifest rather than a broken row -- and all four have
# ZERO rows on the world this was measured against, which is why they are
# refused rather than answered.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- say --------------------------------------------------------------------
action  1  talk                    text0 text1 text2
action  4  play_sound              sound - -
action  5  emote                   emote - -
action  9  random_sound            a b c
action 10  random_emote            a b c

# -- appearance -------------------------------------------------------------
action  2  set_faction             faction flags -
action  3  morph_to_entry_or_model - - -                form=entry_or_model
action 43  mount_to_entry_or_model - - -                form=entry_or_model
action 36  update_template         entry faction -
action 47  stand_state             state - -

# -- combat -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The creature acts ON the selected unit: the buddy becomes the target and the
# creature keeps acting.
action 11  cast_spell              spell select flags   buddy_as_target
action 12  temp_summon_creature    entry select despawn_delay  buddy_as_target
action 32  temp_summon_creature    entry select -       buddy_as_target form=summon_spawn
action 49  temp_summon_creature    entry select -       buddy_as_target form=summon_spawn

# The one verb whose columns are reversed, and the selected unit is the one
# losing the aura rather than something the creature acts through -- so no
# buddy_as_target: the buddy replaces the source.
action 28  remove_aura             select spell -

action 13  threat_change           percent select -     buddy_as_target all=0
action 14  threat_change           percent - -          all=1

action 20  auto_attack             enable - -
action 21  combat_movement         enable melee -
action 29  ranged_movement         distance angle -
action 48  change_movement         type wander_distance -
action 24  evade                   - - -
action 25  flee_for_assist         - - -
action 37  die                     - - -
action 38  zone_combat_pulse       - - -
action 39  call_for_help           radius - -
action 41  despawn_self            delay - -
action 42  set_invincibility       hp percent -
action 40  set_sheath              state - -

# -- phases -----------------------------------------------------------------
action 22  set_phase               phase - -
action 23  inc_phase               by - -
action 30  random_phase            a b c
action 31  random_phase_range      min max -

# -- the unit itself --------------------------------------------------------
# These act ON the selected unit, so no buddy_as_target: the buddy replaces the
# source, and the body's source is the unit that changes.
action 17  set_unit_field          field value select
action 18  set_unit_flag           value select -
action 19  remove_unit_flag        value select -

# -- quest credit -----------------------------------------------------------
# All of these hand the credit to a PLAYER, which is the target.
action 15  quest_event             quest select -       buddy_as_target all=0
action 26  quest_event             quest all -
action 16  cast_event              creature spell select buddy_as_target all=0
action 27  cast_event              creature spell -     all=1
action 33  killed_monster          creature select -    buddy_as_target

# -- instances and AI events ------------------------------------------------
action 34  set_instance_data       field value -
action 35  set_instance_data_guid  field select -       buddy_as_target
action 45  throw_ai_event          event radius -
action 46  set_throw_mask          mask - -

# -- what nothing here can say ----------------------------------------------
refuse  6  unused in this schema -- EventAI's own header says so
refuse  7  unused in this schema -- EventAI's own header says so
refuse  8  unused in this schema -- EventAI's own header says so
refuse 44  carries a chance of its own, and chance in MAI belongs to the rule rather than to one of its steps
refuse 50  names a creature by bare guid with no entry, and the buddy-by-guid search needs the entry to build one
